	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Kingdom of Stormwind is the greatest human realm left standing in the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link}. Its heart is the white city of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}, and around it lie the forests of {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn{/link}, the fields of {link:westfall}Westfall{/link}, the hills of {link:redridge-mountains}Redridge{/link} and the shadowed woods of {link:duskwood}Duskwood{/link}. Twice broken and twice rebuilt, it now leads the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}. Yet its throne is empty, its army is far from home, and its borders are full of enemies.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[When the empire of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} began to come apart, the last heirs of the {link:arathi-highlands}Arathi{/link} bloodline left the old capital of {link:stromgarde-keep}Strom{/link} and went south. In a green and sheltered land they founded a new kingdom and named it {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}. Its capital was {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}. The kingdom grew rich and self-sufficient, and for many centuries it stood apart from the quarrels of the northern realms. The faith of the {link:holy-light}Holy Light{/link} took deep root there, and the clerics of {link:northshire-abbey}Northshire{/link} kept its oldest books.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The First War.{/b} The orcish {link:horde}Horde{/link} came through the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} into the southern marshes, and the kingdom of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} bore the whole weight of the {link:first-war}First War{/link}. Its farms and villages burned. At last {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} itself fell, and King {link:llane-wrynn}Llane Wrynn{/link} was slain in his own keep. Sir {link:anduin-lothar}Anduin Lothar{/link} led the survivors across the sea to {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, with the king's young son {link:varian-wrynn}Varian{/link} among them.
• {b}The Second War.{/b} Lothar's warning moved King {link:terenas-menethil}Terenas Menethil{/link} to raise the {link:alliance}Alliance of Lordaeron{/link}. The exiles of Stormwind fought in the {link:second-war}Second War{/link} beside the northern kingdoms until the Horde was broken.
• {b}The Rebuilding.{/b} The exiles came home to ruins. Varian was crowned king, and the {link:stonemasons-guild}Stonemasons' Guild{/link} raised the city anew from its rubble. When the {link:house-of-nobles}House of Nobles{/link} refused to pay the masons, riots filled the streets, and Queen {link:tiffin-wrynn}Tiffin Wrynn{/link} died in the chaos. The masons were driven out, and from them the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias Brotherhood{/link} was born.
• {b}The Third War.{/b} While the plague destroyed Lordaeron, Stormwind was spared the worst of the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}. When the northern kingdom fell, Stormwind became the first power of the Alliance.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} is a kingdom without its king. {link:varian-wrynn}Varian Wrynn{/link} has vanished, and none can say where he has gone. Highlord {link:bolvar-fordragon}Bolvar Fordragon{/link} rules as regent in the name of the boy prince, {link:anduin-wrynn}Anduin Wrynn{/link}. At court, Lady {link:katrana-prestor}Katrana Prestor{/link} has won the ear of the nobles and much of the regent's trust. The army has marched far from home, and the kingdom's heartland must be held by thin garrisons and volunteers. {link:westfall}Westfall{/link} has fallen to the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias{/link}. {link:riverpaw-gnolls}Gnolls{/link} and {link:kobolds}kobolds{/link} prey upon {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn{/link}, orcs of the {link:blackrock-clan}Blackrock clan{/link} press on {link:redridge-mountains}Redridge{/link}, and the dead walk in {link:duskwood}Duskwood{/link}. Agents of {link:si-7}SI:7{/link} work in the shadows, but the realm's troubles are many and its defenders few.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "arathor",
	title = "Arathor",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Arathor was the first nation of {link:humans}humankind{/link}. It was forged in war against the trolls, and it was saved by an alliance with the elves. From it came every human kingdom of the north and the south. Arathor itself has been gone for more than a thousand years, but its blood and its banners are still remembered wherever humans rule.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[Nearly three thousand years before the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link}, the human tribes of the north were scattered and at war with one another. The Amani {link:trolls}trolls{/link} raided them without mercy. Then {link:thoradin}Thoradin{/link}, warlord of the {link:arathi-highlands}Arathi{/link} tribe, resolved that humankind must unite or perish. By marriage, by promise and by the sword, he brought the tribes under one banner. He named his realm Arathor, and he raised its capital, the fortress-city of {link:stromgarde-keep}Strom{/link}, in the highlands that still bear the Arathi name.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Troll Wars.{/b} When the Amani fell upon {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}, the elves sent envoys to {link:stromgarde-keep}Strom{/link}. In return for the swords of Arathor, they agreed to teach one hundred humans the ways of {link:arcane-magic}magic{/link}. Together, elves and men broke the Amani at the foot of the {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac Mountains{/link}. The {link:troll-wars}Troll Wars{/link} ended, and the elves swore lasting friendship to {link:thoradin}Thoradin{/link}'s line.
• {b}The Expansion.{/b} After Thoradin, the people of Arathor spread far beyond Strom. They founded {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link}, the harbors of {link:gilneas}Gilneas{/link}, the island realm of {link:kul-tiras}Kul Tiras{/link}, the mountain seat of Alterac and the rich lands of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. Each city grew stronger, and each grew more its own master.
• {b}The Fracturing.{/b} Strom, poor in land and trade, slowly lost its hold. Its great families moved north to Lordaeron. The last heirs of the {link:arathi-highlands}Arathi{/link} line sailed south and founded the kingdom that became the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link}. Strom was left to a few ruling houses, who renamed it Stromgarde. The empire had become seven kingdoms.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[Arathor lives on only in its heirs. The seven kingdoms were joined again once, in the {link:alliance}Alliance of Lordaeron{/link}, under {link:anduin-lothar}Anduin Lothar{/link}, last of {link:thoradin}Thoradin{/link}'s blood. Today the highlands of {link:stromgarde-keep}Strom{/link} are a land of ruins, fought over by orcs, trolls, ogres and the brigands of the {link:syndicate}Syndicate{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "lordaeron",
	title = "Lordaeron",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Lordaeron was the mightiest of the human kingdoms. From its {link:capital-city}Capital City{/link} in the glades of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link}, its kings ruled the northern lands and led the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} that saved humankind in the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}. It fell in the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, betrayed from within by its own prince. Its lands are now the kingdom of the dead.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[In the days of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link}, settlers claimed the fertile glades of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link} and named the land after Lordain, a general of the {link:troll-wars}Troll Wars{/link}. When {link:stromgarde-keep}Strom{/link} declined, many of its noble families moved their estates north to these rich fields. They made Lordaeron a kingdom in its own right, and its borders grew quickly. Lordaeron was also a land of faith. Pilgrims came from far away to its monasteries in search of healing and wisdom in the {link:holy-light}Holy Light{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} When Sir {link:anduin-lothar}Anduin Lothar{/link} brought the survivors of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} north, King {link:terenas-menethil}Terenas Menethil{/link} took them in. He then summoned the rulers of the human kingdoms and raised the {link:alliance}Alliance of Lordaeron{/link}. Under Lothar's command, it drove the {link:horde}Horde{/link} back through the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link}.
• {b}The Uneasy Peace.{/b} The defeated orcs were kept in internment camps across Lordaeron, at great cost. The burden split the Alliance. {link:gilneas}Gilneas{/link}, {link:stromgarde-keep}Stromgarde{/link} and {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} left it, and Terenas's kingdom was weakened.
• {b}The Plague.{/b} In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, the {link:cult-of-the-damned}Cult of the Damned{/link} spread a plague through the grain of the northern lands, and the dead rose in their thousands. Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} burned the plagued city of Stratholme in the {link:culling-of-stratholme}Culling{/link}, then pursued the plague's masters to Northrend. He returned as a death knight of the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} and slew his father on his throne. That was the {link:fall-of-lordaeron}Fall of Lordaeron{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[Lordaeron is a kingdom of corpses. The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} holds the Plaguelands. Beneath the ruins of {link:capital-city}Capital City{/link}, the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} of {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas Windrunner{/link} have made the {link:undercity}Undercity{/link} their home. The {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} burns all it suspects of plague, and the {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link} stands against the Scourge beside any who will help. No king of the living rules here any longer.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "gilneas",
	title = "Gilneas",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Gilneas is a proud human kingdom on a rugged peninsula south of {link:silverpine-forest}Silverpine{/link}. Its people are hardy and self-reliant, and its army was once among the strongest of the seven kingdoms. After the {link:second-war}Second War{/link} its king shut his realm away from the world behind a great wall. What passes behind that wall, no outsider can say.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[Gilneas was one of the city-states founded by the people of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} after the {link:troll-wars}Troll Wars{/link}. Its settlers built strong harbors along the coast, and its boldest sailors went on to found {link:kul-tiras}Kul Tiras{/link}. Unable to rival the Kul Tiran fleet, Gilneas turned to trade and to arms. Its soldiers were counted equal to any in Arathor.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} {link:genn-greymane}King Genn Greymane{/link} joined the Alliance of Lordaeron with little love for it. He believed that Gilneas could defend itself alone, and he kept his armies close to home.
• {b}{link:the-greymane-wall}The Greymane Wall{/link}.{/b} After the war, the cost of the orcish internment camps angered him. Greymane withdrew Gilneas from the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}. He then raised a vast wall across the northern border of his kingdom and closed its gates. The wall cut through the lands of his own nobles, leaving villages such as {link:pyrewood-village}Pyrewood{/link} and {link:ambermill}Ambermill{/link} outside it.
• {b}The {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} When the plague swept {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, the gates of Gilneas stayed shut. No army came out of the south to help the dying kingdom.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:the-greymane-wall}The Greymane Wall{/link} still stands, and its gates are still closed. Beyond it, in {link:silverpine-forest}Silverpine Forest{/link}, the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} and the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} contend for the old lands of the north. The villagers left outside the wall must fend for themselves. What has become of the kingdom within is not known.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "kul-tiras",
	title = "Kul Tiras",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Kul Tiras is an island kingdom in the Great Sea, west of Khaz Modan. It is a nation of sailors and shipwrights, and its navy was once the greatest in the world. From the house of Proudmoore came its admirals, and from its harbors came the fleets that carried the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} to war.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[Sailors from {link:gilneas}Gilneas{/link} discovered a large island to the south, rich in ore and timber. Some of them stayed and founded a maritime outpost there, which grew into a kingdom of its own. Kul Tiras prospered on fishing and trade. Its merchant fleets sailed every coast of the known world, and in the days of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} it held the largest navy of the empire.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} Lord Admiral {link:daelin-proudmoore}Daelin Proudmoore{/link} brought the fleets of Kul Tiras into the {link:alliance}Alliance of Lordaeron{/link}. His ships fought the orcish fleets on the seas and kept the Alliance's armies supplied. The kingdom paid a heavy price in ships and men.
• {b}The Uneasy Peace.{/b} When the Alliance weakened after the war, Kul Tiras remained loyal to it, but it drew back more and more into its own affairs.
• {b}{link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link}.{/b} After the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, Daelin's daughter, {link:jaina-proudmoore}Jaina Proudmoore{/link}, led the survivors of the north to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, where she made peace with the orcs of {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}. Daelin would not accept it. He came with his fleet to destroy the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, and he was slain in the fighting before the walls of Theramore.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[Kul Tiras stands far away across the sea, and it takes little part in the affairs of the mainland. On the coasts of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, Kul Tiran marines still hold {link:northwatch-hold}Northwatch Hold{/link} in {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link} and {link:tiragarde-keep}Tiragarde Keep{/link} in {link:durotar}Durotar{/link}. They have not forgiven the {link:horde}Horde{/link} for the death of their admiral.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "dalaran",
	title = "Dalaran",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Dalaran is {link:city-of-dalaran}the city of the magi{/link}. It was the first city-state of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} to rule itself, and for more than two thousand years it was the heart of human magic. Its violet towers rose above the shores of Lordamere Lake until the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} and the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} cast them down. Now Dalaran has risen again in the {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac Mountains{/link}, and its magi are its lords.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[Dalaran began as a trading post in the middle of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link}. It grew quickly, and it became a refuge for the empire's magi, who were distrusted by common folk. Under the mage Ardogan, the city won its freedom from {link:stromgarde-keep}Strom{/link} and was governed by sorcerers. Their reckless magic drew the notice of demons. To fight them in secret, the magi of Dalaran and the elves of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} founded {link:shadow-council}the Council{/link} of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link}, whose Guardians defended the world for generations. In time the city's magi formed the {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link}, who came to rule it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} Dalaran joined the {link:alliance}Alliance of Lordaeron{/link} and sent its magi to fight the orcs. After the war, its wizards watched the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} from {link:nethergarde-keep}Nethergarde Keep{/link}.
• {b}The {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} The necromancer {link:kel-thuzad}Kel'Thuzad{/link}, once a mage of Dalaran, founded the {link:cult-of-the-damned}Cult of the Damned{/link}. At his bidding, {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} led the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} against the city and seized the spellbook of {link:medivh}Medivh{/link}. With it, {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} was summoned into the world. The demon lord crushed Dalaran with a single spell and left it in ruins.
• {b}The Rebuilding.{/b} The surviving magi returned to the ruins. They raised a great violet barrier over the city and rebuilt it behind that shield, hidden from the world.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[Dalaran stands rebuilt in the {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac Mountains{/link}, and its barrier is gone. No one outside the {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link} can yet say why it fell. The city is open once more, and its streets are full of magi, merchants and bankers. But all is not well within. Enchantments go wrong, arcane constructs run wild, and demonic energy stirs in the streets. The Kirin Tor are proud, and they do not willingly admit that they need help.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "kirin-tor",
	title = "Kirin Tor",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Kirin Tor are the magi of {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} and the rulers of that city. They are the keepers of human magic: its scholars, its judges and its wardens. They have long claimed the right to watch over every spell cast in the human lands, and they guard their secrets jealously.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[When the empire of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} began to break apart, the magi of {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} formed a sect to study and record every spell and magical relic known to humankind. That sect was the Kirin Tor. It grew into the ruling order of the city, led by a council of its greatest members. From their Violet Citadel they judged which magic might be practised, and which must be forbidden.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Guardians.{/b} For centuries the Kirin Tor worked alongside {link:shadow-council}the Council{/link} of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link}, which chose the Guardians who fought demons in secret. The last Guardian was {link:medivh}Medivh{/link}.
• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} The magi of the Kirin Tor fought for the {link:alliance}Alliance of Lordaeron{/link}. After the war, they built {link:nethergarde-keep}Nethergarde Keep{/link} near the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} to watch the ruined land beyond it.
• {b}The {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} The Kirin Tor had expelled the mage {link:kel-thuzad}Kel'Thuzad{/link} for his study of necromancy. He returned as master of the {link:cult-of-the-damned}Cult of the Damned{/link}, and his plague destroyed {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. Archmage Antonidas, the head of the order, was slain when the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} took {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link}.
• {b}The Worgen.{/b} One mage of the order, {link:archmage-arugal}Archmage Arugal{/link}, summoned the savage worgen to fight the Scourge in {link:silverpine-forest}Silverpine Forest{/link}. They proved as great a curse as the undead. Arugal now holds {link:shadowfang-keep}Shadowfang Keep{/link}, and his mind is said to be lost.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The Kirin Tor have rebuilt {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} in the {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac Mountains{/link}, and its barrier has fallen. Within the city, their spells misfire and their constructs slip their bonds, and they struggle to keep control of their own streets. Their magi still keep watch at {link:nethergarde-keep}Nethergarde{/link}, and some of their number stand with {link:jaina-proudmoore}Jaina Proudmoore{/link} in {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "quel-thalas",
	title = "Quel'Thalas",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Quel'Thalas is the kingdom of the {link:high-elves}high elves{/link}, in the northern forests of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. For thousands of years it was a realm of eternal spring, fed by the magic of the Sunwell. In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link} the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} marched through its gates and defiled its sacred fount. What remains of the kingdom lies silent and far away.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[After the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}, a band of Highborne exiles left {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, banished by the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} for their love of magic. Led by Dath'Remar Sunstrider, they crossed the sea and settled in the north of the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link}. There they founded Quel'Thalas and raised the Sunwell, a fount of arcane power. Runestones were set about the forests to hide their magic from the demons it might draw.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:troll-wars}Troll Wars{/link}.{/b} The Amani trolls nearly overran the young kingdom. The elves sought help from {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} and taught magic to a hundred humans in exchange for its armies. Together they broke the Amani, and the elves swore friendship to the line of {link:thoradin}Thoradin{/link}.
• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} When the {link:horde}Horde{/link} and the Amani set the forests ablaze, King Anasterian Sunstrider honored his old debt and joined the {link:alliance}Alliance of Lordaeron{/link}. After the war, he judged that the Alliance had failed his people, and he withdrew from it.
• {b}The {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} led the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} north. Ranger-General {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas Windrunner{/link} fought him at every gate and was slain. Arthas killed King Anasterian and used the Sunwell to raise {link:kel-thuzad}Kel'Thuzad{/link} as a lich. The heart of the elven realm was defiled.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[Quel'Thalas lies beyond the Plaguelands, cut off from the south by the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}. Few messages come from it. The high elves who remain in the southern lands live in small, scattered bands, such as the rangers of {link:quel-danil-lodge}Quel'Danil Lodge{/link} in {link:the-hinterlands}The Hinterlands{/link}. Many of them grieve for a home they may not see again.]=],
		},
	},
})

