		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Alliance is the league of peoples bound together against their common enemies. {link:humans}Humans{/link}, {link:dwarves}dwarves{/link}, {link:gnomes}gnomes{/link} and {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} stand within it. It was born in the {link:second-war}Second War{/link} to face the orcish {link:horde}Horde{/link}, and it has been broken and remade since. Today its greatest powers are the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link} and the {link:kingdom-of-ironforge}Kingdom of Ironforge{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[When {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} fell in the {link:first-war}First War{/link}, Sir {link:anduin-lothar}Anduin Lothar{/link} brought its survivors to {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} and warned that the {link:horde}Horde{/link} would come north. King {link:terenas-menethil}Terenas Menethil{/link} heeded him. He summoned the rulers of the human kingdoms and bound them into the Alliance of Lordaeron, with Lothar as its supreme commander. The dwarves of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}, the gnomes of {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link} and the high elves of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} joined it too.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} The Alliance met the {link:horde}Horde{/link} across the north and pushed it back to {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock{/link} Spire. {link:anduin-lothar}Lothar{/link} fell in the last battles, and his lieutenant {link:turalyon}Turalyon{/link} led the final victory. The orcs who survived were herded into internment camps.
• {b}The Breaking.{/b} The cost of the camps and old grievances split the Alliance. {link:gilneas}Gilneas{/link}, {link:stromgarde-keep}Stromgarde{/link} and {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} left it. {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac{/link} had already betrayed it to the Horde and been stripped of its crown.
• {b}The {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} The plague and the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} destroyed {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. {link:jaina-proudmoore}Jaina Proudmoore{/link} led survivors west to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, where humans, orcs and night elves fought side by side at the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}.
• {b}The New Alliance.{/b} In the years since, {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} has taken up the banner that Lordaeron dropped. {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} stands with it, the gnomes of fallen {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link} shelter among the dwarves, and the night elves of {link:darnassus}Darnassus{/link} have joined it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The Alliance is strong on paper and stretched thin in truth. King {link:varian-wrynn}Varian Wrynn{/link} has vanished, and Highlord {link:bolvar-fordragon}Bolvar Fordragon{/link} rules {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} as regent. King {link:magni-bronzebeard}Magni Bronzebeard{/link} rules {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}. {link:tyrande-whisperwind}Tyrande Whisperwind{/link} leads the night elves, and {link:jaina-proudmoore}Jaina Proudmoore{/link} holds {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link}. Their soldiers fight the {link:horde}Horde{/link} in {link:ashenvale}Ashenvale{/link} and the {link:the-barrens}Barrens{/link}, the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} in {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} and a dozen lesser enemies at home. Peace with the orcs is often spoken of, and seldom trusted.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "horde",
	title = "Horde",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Horde is the league of the orcs and their allies: the {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear trolls{/link}, the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} and the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}. It was born on another world as a tool of demons. It crossed into {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}, burned kingdoms and was broken. Then it was reborn under a young warchief as a people seeking freedom. Its capital is {link:orgrimmar}Orgrimmar{/link}, in the red land of {link:durotar}Durotar{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[On the world of Draenor, the orcs were a proud people of clans and shamans. The demon {link:kil-jaeden}Kil'jaeden{/link} of the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} set out to make them his weapon. Through the shaman {link:ner-zhul}Ner'zhul{/link} and then the warlock {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link}, he taught them fel magic. At last the clan chieftains drank the blood of the demon {link:mannoroth}Mannoroth{/link}, and a burning bloodlust bound them to the Legion. United as one Horde, they destroyed the draenei, and their world withered beneath them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:first-war}First War{/link}.{/b} Through the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link}, the Horde invaded the kingdom of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} and destroyed it. {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} fell, and King {link:llane-wrynn}Llane Wrynn{/link} was slain.
• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} Under Warchief {link:orgrim-doomhammer}Orgrim Doomhammer{/link}, the Horde marched north with ogres, Amani trolls, goblins and enslaved red dragons. The {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} defeated it, and most of the surviving orcs were locked in internment camps.
• {b}The New Horde.{/b} In the camps, the orcs sank into a strange lethargy. A young {link:orcs}orc{/link} raised as a slave, {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}, broke free, learned the old ways of the shaman and set his people free. Doomhammer died fighting beside him and passed him his hammer and his title.
• {b}The {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} Heeding the prophet {link:medivh}Medivh{/link}, Thrall led the Horde to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. There he won the friendship of the {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} and the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} of {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne Bloodhoof{/link}. {link:grom-hellscream}Grom Hellscream{/link} slew {link:mannoroth}Mannoroth{/link} and freed the orcs from his blood curse. The Horde fought beside the Alliance at the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:thrall}Thrall{/link} rules as Warchief from {link:orgrimmar}Orgrimmar{/link}, named in honor of Doomhammer. {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne{/link} leads the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} from {link:thunder-bluff}Thunder Bluff{/link}, {link:vol-jin}Vol'jin{/link} leads the {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link}, and {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas Windrunner{/link} brings the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} to the Horde's side. The peace with {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link} holds, but only just. In {link:ashenvale}Ashenvale{/link}, orcs cut timber in the night elves' forests and blood is spilled for it. Kul Tiran marines guard the coasts, centaurs and {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link} press on every border, and the demon cult of the {link:burning-blade}Burning Blade{/link} festers within {link:durotar}Durotar{/link} itself.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "burning-legion",
	title = "Burning Legion",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Burning Legion is a vast army of demons that has laid waste to countless worlds. Its master is {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link}, a fallen titan who once defended creation and now seeks to unmake it. Three times the Legion has reached for {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}. Three times it has been thrown back, at a terrible cost.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[{link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link} was once the greatest champion of the titans, the makers of worlds. Over ages of war against the demons of the Twisting Nether, he came to believe that all creation was flawed and must be burned. He turned against his own kind and gathered an army of demons to do it. Among the first he corrupted were the eredar, whose leaders {link:kil-jaeden}Kil'jaeden{/link} and {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} became his chief lieutenants.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The War of the Ancients.{/b} {link:queen-azshara}Queen Azshara{/link} and her Highborne drew the Legion into the world through the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link}. The night elves, led by {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion Stormrage{/link}, fought back in the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}. The destruction of the Well shattered the continent in the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link} and cut the demons off.
• {b}The Horde.{/b} {link:kil-jaeden}Kil'jaeden{/link} then corrupted the orcs of Draenor and made them a weapon. The {link:horde}Horde{/link} he forged was cast against {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} in the {link:first-war}First War{/link} and the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.
• {b}The {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} The Legion made the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} to prepare the way. The plague killed {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, and {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} himself was summoned into the world at {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link}. He marched on the World Tree, {link:nordrassil}Nordrassil{/link}. At the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, the night elves, humans and orcs held him long enough for the spirits of the ancients to destroy him.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} is dead, but the Legion is not gone from {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}. Demons still haunt the corrupted woods of {link:felwood}Felwood{/link}, the ruins of {link:azshara}Azshara{/link} and the wastes of {link:desolace}Desolace{/link}. The cult of the {link:burning-blade}Burning Blade{/link} serves them in secret among the orcs. In the {link:blasted-lands}Blasted Lands{/link}, the magi of {link:nethergarde-keep}Nethergarde{/link} watch the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} for any sign of their return.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "scourge",
	title = "Scourge",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Scourge is an army of the undead, raised by plague and ruled by the Lich King in the ice of Northrend. In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link} it destroyed the kingdom of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, defiled {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} and razed {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link}. It still holds much of the north, and it still hungers for the living.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[After the orcs failed him, {link:kil-jaeden}Kil'jaeden{/link} of the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} punished their old shaman {link:ner-zhul}Ner'zhul{/link}. He tore away the {link:orcs}orc{/link}'s body and bound his spirit into a suit of armor sealed in a block of ice. Then he cast him into Northrend and named him the Lich King. His task was to spread a plague of undeath across the human lands and prepare them for the Legion. From his Frozen Throne, the Lich King reached out with his mind to the living, and he drew the ambitious and the desperate to his side.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Plague.{/b} The mage {link:kel-thuzad}Kel'Thuzad{/link} heard the Lich King's call and founded the {link:cult-of-the-damned}Cult of the Damned{/link}. Through the cult, the plague was spread in the grain of northern {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. Those who ate it died and rose again as undead.
• {b}The Fall.{/b} Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} hunted the plague to Northrend. There he took up the runeblade Frostmourne and became the Lich King's champion. He returned to murder his father and deliver Lordaeron to the dead. He then led the Scourge through {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}, where he raised Kel'Thuzad as a lich, and on to {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link}, where the demon lord {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} was summoned.
• {b}The Breaking of the Chains.{/b} After Archimonde fell at {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link}, the Lich King's hold weakened. Many of the undead broke free, and {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas Windrunner{/link} led them as the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}. Arthas went north to the Lich King's aid.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The Scourge still rules the Plaguelands. {link:kel-thuzad}Kel'Thuzad{/link} commands in the Lich King's name, and his servants hold the ruined city of Stratholme, the school of necromancy at Scholomance and many a fallen town. Plagued creatures stalk the woods, and abominations guard the dead lands. Against them stand the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}, the {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} and the {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link}, who agree on nothing else.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "cult-of-the-damned",
	title = "Cult of the Damned",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Cult of the Damned is the living priesthood of the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}. Its members worship the Lich King and serve him willingly, in the hope of eternal life after death. It was the cult that carried the plague into {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, and its necromancers still raise the dead in the Lich King's name.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The cult was founded by {link:kel-thuzad}Kel'Thuzad{/link}, a mage of the {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link} who was cast out for his forbidden study of necromancy. He journeyed to Northrend and heard the voice of the Lich King. He returned to {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} as its prophet. Among the poor and the forgotten of the north, he preached a new society, where all would be equal and where death would be no end. Thousands followed him, and few understood what they had joined.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Plague.{/b} The cult spread a plague of undeath through the granaries of northern {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. From {link:ruins-of-andorhal}Andorhal{/link}, tainted grain went out to the villages, and the dead began to rise.
• {b}{link:kel-thuzad}Kel'Thuzad{/link}'s Death and Return.{/b} Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} slew Kel'Thuzad at Andorhal. After Arthas fell into the Lich King's service, he carried the necromancer's remains to the Sunwell of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} and raised him as a lich.
• {b}Scholomance.{/b} The Barov family gave their island keep of {link:caer-darrow}Caer Darrow{/link} to the cult. There, in the Scholomance, the cult trains new necromancers.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The cult remains strong in the Plaguelands. Its acolytes serve in the ruins of Stratholme and {link:ruins-of-andorhal}Andorhal{/link}. In the Scholomance, the Darkmaster Gandling teaches necromancy to willing students. The cult's agents still move among the living, in search of new recruits and new ways to spread the plague.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "scarlet-crusade",
	title = "Scarlet Crusade",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Scarlet Crusade is a militant order of the {link:holy-light}Holy Light{/link}, sworn to destroy the undead of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. It was born from the grief of the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, and it has grown harsh and fanatical. The Crusade trusts no one. It hunts the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}, but it also hunts the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}, and it treats any outsider as a possible carrier of the plague.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[After the {link:fall-of-lordaeron}Fall of Lordaeron{/link}, the order of paladins founded by {link:uther-the-lightbringer}Uther the Lightbringer{/link} lay broken, and many of its knights were dead. Survivors gathered under Grand Crusader Saidan Dathrohan, a paladin of the old order. They swore to cleanse {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} of every trace of the plague, and they took scarlet as their color. Many who had lost everything to the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} flocked to their banners.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Crusade.{/b} The Crusade fought the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} across the north with great courage and little mercy. It fortified the {link:scarlet-monastery}Scarlet Monastery{/link} in {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal Glades{/link}, the town of {link:hearthglen}Hearthglen{/link} and the city of {link:tyr-s-hand}Tyr's Hand{/link}.
• {b}The Zealots.{/b} In time, the Crusade's fervor turned to cruelty. It began to purge anyone it suspected of the plague, and its inquisitors grew feared among the living. Some of its members could not bear what it had become. They left it and founded the {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The Scarlet Crusade holds the Monastery in {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link}, where {link:high-inquisitor-whitemane}High Inquisitor Whitemane{/link} and {link:scarlet-commander-mograine}Scarlet Commander Mograine{/link} lead its knights. Its forces also hold {link:hearthglen}Hearthglen{/link} in the {link:western-plaguelands}Western Plaguelands{/link} and {link:tyr-s-hand}Tyr's Hand{/link} in the {link:eastern-plaguelands}Eastern Plaguelands{/link}. Its patrols burn the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} wherever they find them. Its zeal is real, and so is its strength. Whether it still serves the Light is a question its own members no longer dare to ask.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "argent-dawn",
	title = "Argent Dawn",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Argent Dawn is an order sworn to defend {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} from the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}, the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} and every other power that would destroy it. It stands apart from kings and warchiefs. It welcomes any who will fight the undead, whatever their race or banner, and so it counts orcs, humans, dwarves and even {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} among its friends.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The Dawn was born of the {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link}. As the Crusade grew fanatical, some of its members came to fear that its leaders had lost their way. {link:lord-maxwell-tyrosus}Lord Maxwell Tyrosus{/link} and others refused to follow it further. They left the Crusade and founded a new order, true to the teachings of the {link:holy-light}Holy Light{/link} as they understood them. Its first leader was Lord Raymond George.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Fight in the North.{/b} From its first days, the Argent Dawn fought the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} across the Plaguelands, often with few soldiers and fewer supplies.
• {b}An Order Open to All.{/b} Unlike the Crusade, the Dawn does not ask who its allies were in life. It accepts the aid of the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and the {link:horde}Horde{/link} alike, and it judges each by deeds alone.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:lord-maxwell-tyrosus}Lord Maxwell Tyrosus{/link} leads the Argent Dawn from {link:light-s-hope-chapel}Light's Hope Chapel{/link} in the {link:eastern-plaguelands}Eastern Plaguelands{/link}. Its camps dot the Plaguelands, and its envoys wait in distant cities to gather allies. The Dawn rewards those who bring proof of the dead they have destroyed. Its members say that the war with the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} will not be won by any one nation alone.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "defias-brotherhood",
	title = "Defias Brotherhood",
	aliases = { "Defias" },
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Defias Brotherhood is an army of outlaws that has seized {link:westfall}Westfall{/link} and preys upon the lands of the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link}. Its members wear red bandanas and strike from the shadows. At its core stand the stonemasons who rebuilt {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} and were never paid for their work. They mean to take what they are owed, and then to take the city itself.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[After the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, the {link:stonemasons-guild}Stonemasons' Guild{/link} of {link:edwin-vancleef}Edwin VanCleef{/link} rebuilt {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} from its ashes. When their work was done, the {link:house-of-nobles}House of Nobles{/link} refused to pay them. The masons rioted, and in the chaos Queen {link:tiffin-wrynn}Tiffin Wrynn{/link} was killed. The masons were driven out of the city. Led by VanCleef, they went west into the hills and fields of {link:westfall}Westfall{/link}, and there they became the Defias Brotherhood.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Conquest of {link:westfall}Westfall{/link}.{/b} With the army far away and the crown silent, the Brotherhood took Westfall almost unopposed. Its members drove farmers from their lands and made the village of {link:moonbrook}Moonbrook{/link} their stronghold.
• {b}The Reach of the Brotherhood.{/b} Defias thieves spread into {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn{/link}, {link:redridge-mountains}Redridge{/link} and {link:duskwood}Duskwood{/link}. Gold stolen by kobolds passes to their agents, and their rings bear the old mark of the masons' guild.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The Brotherhood rules {link:westfall}Westfall{/link} from the shadows. Beneath {link:moonbrook}Moonbrook{/link}, in the {link:the-deadmines}Deadmines{/link}, {link:edwin-vancleef}VanCleef{/link}'s masons build a great ship for a purpose they keep secret. Their {link:harvest-golems}harvest golems{/link} work stolen fields, and their gangs hold the roads. Only the People's Militia of {link:sentinel-hill}Sentinel Hill{/link}, led by {link:gryan-stoutmantle}Gryan Stoutmantle{/link}, stands against them. In {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}'s prison, the {link:the-stockade}Stockade{/link}, captured Defias have risen and taken the cells for themselves.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "stonemasons-guild",
	title = "Stonemasons' Guild",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Stonemasons' Guild was the brotherhood of builders who raised {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} anew after the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}. Their skill gave the city its white walls and great towers. The kingdom's betrayal of them turned its master masons into its most dangerous enemies.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[When the exiles of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} returned from {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, they found their capital in ruins. The work of rebuilding fell to the stonemasons. Their master, {link:edwin-vancleef}Edwin VanCleef{/link}, was a craftsman of rare gifts, and under him the guild accomplished in years what might have taken generations. The city that stands today is largely their work.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Betrayal.{/b} When the work was done, the {link:house-of-nobles}House of Nobles{/link} refused to pay the masons what they were owed. The masons protested, and the protest became a riot. Queen {link:tiffin-wrynn}Tiffin Wrynn{/link} was killed in the chaos.
• {b}The Exile.{/b} The masons were driven from {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}. {link:edwin-vancleef}VanCleef{/link} led them west, where they became the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias Brotherhood{/link}. The skills that built a city were turned to raising fortresses for thieves.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The old guild's mark survives on {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias{/link} rings and in the stonework of the {link:the-deadmines}Deadmines{/link}. Across {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn{/link} and {link:westfall}Westfall{/link}, the masons now build for the Brotherhood. {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}'s walls still stand as the best proof of what the guild could do.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Unrecorded",
			text = [=[No chronicle tells what became of the masons who did not follow {link:edwin-vancleef}VanCleef{/link} into exile, or whether any guild of masons still works in {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} today.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "house-of-nobles",
	title = "House of Nobles",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The House of Nobles is the assembly of the great lords of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}. Its members hold lands, wealth and old titles, and they have long had a hand in the kingdom's treasury and its laws. It was their refusal to pay the stonemasons that set the kingdom on the road to its present troubles.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records when the House of Nobles first gathered. It is as old as the noble families of the kingdom, and it has endured through fire and exile. When {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} was rebuilt after the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, the House stood at the side of the young King {link:varian-wrynn}Varian Wrynn{/link}, and its voice carried great weight in the new court.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Masons' Wages.{/b} The {link:stonemasons-guild}Stonemasons' Guild{/link} rebuilt the capital under {link:edwin-vancleef}Edwin VanCleef{/link}. When the work was done, the House of Nobles refused to pay the masons what they were owed. The masons' protest turned to riot, and Queen {link:tiffin-wrynn}Tiffin Wrynn{/link} died in the violence. The masons were exiled, and they became the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias Brotherhood{/link}.
• {b}Blame.{/b} Many in {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} still blame the nobles for the queen's death and for the Defias. The nobles, for their part, blame the masons.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[With {link:varian-wrynn}King Varian{/link} gone, the nobles have great influence over the regency of Highlord {link:bolvar-fordragon}Bolvar Fordragon{/link}. Lady {link:katrana-prestor}Katrana Prestor{/link} has become a favorite among them, and her counsel is heard in every debate. Commoners mutter that the lords argue over taxes while {link:westfall}Westfall{/link} burns. The regent must keep the nobles content, and it does not make his task easier.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "si-7",
	title = "SI:7",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[SI:7 is the secret service of the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link}. Its agents are spies, scouts and assassins who serve the crown in silence. They watch the kingdom's enemies, both outside its walls and within them. Few in {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} know much about them, and that is how they prefer it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records when SI:7 was founded or who first gave it its name. It has served the kings of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} since before the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, and its agents have always worked far from the light of the court.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}In the Shadows.{/b} SI:7 has hunted the kingdom's hidden enemies for many years. It has watched rival kingdoms, traitors at home and dangerous cults. Its members are drawn chiefly from the rogues of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}, who are trained at its headquarters.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:master-mathias-shaw}Master Mathias Shaw{/link} leads SI:7 from its headquarters in {link:old-town}Old Town{/link}, in {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind City{/link}. His agents follow the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias Brotherhood{/link} across {link:westfall}Westfall{/link}, watch the Brotherhood's allies and report on strange doings among the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}. Some serve in {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link} to guard {link:jaina-proudmoore}Jaina Proudmoore{/link}'s rule. Others have joined the rogues of {link:ravenholdt-manor}Ravenholdt{/link} in the war against the {link:syndicate}Syndicate{/link}. With the king gone and the army abroad, Shaw's quiet work is more important than ever.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "explorers-league",
	title = "Explorers' League",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Explorers' League is a society of dwarven scholars and adventurers based in {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}. Its members dig for relics, map forgotten ruins and study the mysteries of the ancient world. Above all, they seek the true origins of the {link:dwarves}dwarven people{/link}, and they believe the answer lies buried in stone.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The dwarves have always delved deep, but the League turned delving into scholarship. From the {link:hall-of-explorers}Hall of Explorers{/link} in {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}, it sends expeditions across the world and gathers what they find. Its members prize knowledge as highly as gold. They are known for their courage, and just as well known for their disregard of danger.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Great Dig.{/b} The League has long believed that the dwarves were shaped from stone by the titans, the makers of the world. Its expeditions have searched ancient ruins across Khaz Modan and beyond for proof of this.
• {b}Famous Names.{/b} Among its members is {link:brann-bronzebeard}Brann Bronzebeard{/link}, brother of King {link:magni-bronzebeard}Magni Bronzebeard{/link}, who is the most celebrated explorer of his age.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:high-explorer-magellas}High Explorer Magellas{/link} leads the League from the {link:hall-of-explorers}Hall of Explorers{/link}. Its dig sites are scattered across the world: at {link:ironband-s-excavation-site}Ironband's Excavation Site{/link} in {link:loch-modan}Loch Modan{/link}, at {link:bael-modan}Bael Modan{/link} in {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link}, and in the ruins of {link:uldaman}Uldaman{/link} in the {link:badlands}Badlands{/link}. In the {link:wetlands}Wetlands{/link}, {link:whelgar-s-excavation-site}Whelgar's Excavation Site{/link} has uncovered something that its diggers were not prepared for. Trogg attacks and rival claims plague many of these sites, but the League does not give up easily.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "cenarion-circle",
	title = "Cenarion Circle",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Cenarion Circle is the order of druids, the keepers of nature. Its members draw their power from the land and from the {link:emerald-dream}Emerald Dream{/link}, and they are sworn to protect the living world. The Circle is named for the demigod {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link}. Long an order of {link:night-elves}night elves{/link}, it now counts {link:tauren}tauren{/link} among its members too.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The first druid of the night elves was {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion Stormrage{/link}, taught by {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link} himself. During the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}, Malfurion and his followers used their new craft against the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}. After the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}, the druids became guardians of the night elves' lands. For thousands of years they slept in the {link:emerald-dream}Emerald Dream{/link}, waking only in times of need.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} The druids were woken to face the Legion once more. They fought at the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, where the World Tree {link:nordrassil}Nordrassil{/link} was sacrificed to destroy {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link}.
• {b}An Open Circle.{/b} In the years since, the Circle has welcomed {link:tauren}tauren{/link} druids, first among them {link:hamuul-runetotem}Hamuul Runetotem{/link}. It stands apart from both the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The Circle's heart is {link:moonglade}Moonglade{/link}, a sacred vale where {link:keeper-remulos}Keeper Remulos{/link}, son of {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link}, holds watch. Its druids tend the wild places of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} and try to heal the corruption of {link:felwood}Felwood{/link}. {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion{/link} has withdrawn into the {link:emerald-dream}Emerald Dream{/link}. In his absence, Arch Druid {link:fandral-staghelm}Fandral Staghelm{/link} leads the druids of {link:darnassus}Darnassus{/link}, where a new World Tree, {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link}, has been grown.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "earthen-ring",
	title = "Earthen Ring",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Earthen Ring is a council of shamans devoted to the balance of the {link:elements}Elements{/link}. Its members listen to the spirits of earth, fire, water and air, and they strive to keep those forces in harmony. The Ring stands above the quarrels of nations. Its eyes are on the world itself.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The Earthen Ring was founded by the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} long ago, to guide their people with wisdom and to keep peace between the elemental spirits. Its elders have met in council for generations. The shamans of the Ring do not command the elements. They ask, and they bargain, and they remember that the spirits are not servants.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The New Shamans.{/b} When {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} brought the orcs back to the ways of the shaman, the paths of the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} and the orcs met. After the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, the Earthen Ring began to welcome orcish and troll shamans into its circles.
• {b}The Forsaken.{/b} When the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} asked to join the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, they claimed to seek a cure for their undeath in the healing powers of the earth. Thrall and {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne Bloodhoof{/link} were wary. It was the Elder Council of the Ring that urged the Horde to help them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The shamans of the Earthen Ring watch over the elements of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} and beyond. They are troubled by what they hear. Fire rages in the depths of {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock{/link}, and the elements grow restless in many lands. {link:muln-earthfury}Muln Earthfury{/link}, a {link:tauren}tauren{/link} of great wisdom, leads the Ring, though he seldom shows himself.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "twilight-s-hammer",
	title = "Twilight's Hammer",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Twilight's Hammer is a cult of doom. It was once an orcish clan of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}. Now it is a fellowship of madmen of every race, who worship ancient powers buried beneath the world and long for the end of all things. Where the cult gathers, strange rites are held in the dark.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The Twilight's Hammer was a clan of the {link:horde}Horde{/link} led by Cho'gall, a two-headed {link:ogres}ogre{/link}-mage who was among {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link}'s closest servants. Even among the orcs, its members were feared as fanatics. They believed that the world was doomed, and that their task was to hasten its end.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Second War.{/b} In the midst of the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link} betrayed the {link:horde}Horde{/link} to seek the Tomb of {link:sargeras}Sargeras{/link}. Cho'gall and his clan followed him. Warchief {link:orgrim-doomhammer}Orgrim Doomhammer{/link} turned his armies on the traitors and broke the clan, and the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} took advantage of the chaos. No chronicle of this age records Cho'gall's fate.
• {b}The Cult Reborn.{/b} The clan did not die. It became a cult devoted to the Old Gods, the dark powers imprisoned deep within {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}. It began to draw in members of many races who shared its hunger for ruin.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The cult works in hidden places. Its members have been found in the flooded ruins of {link:blackfathom-deeps}Blackfathom Deeps{/link} in {link:ashenvale}Ashenvale{/link}, where they perform dark rites among the {link:naga}naga{/link}. Its camps are said to lie in the desert of {link:silithus}Silithus{/link}, far to the south. No one knows how many serve the Hammer, or how close its members stand to the thrones of the world.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "burning-blade",
	title = "Burning Blade",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Burning Blade was once an orcish clan of fearsome swordsmen. Now it is chiefly a cult of demon worshippers that hides among the orcs of the new {link:horde}Horde{/link}. Its members serve the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} and work to drag their people back into the corruption from which {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} freed them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[On Draenor, the Burning Blade was a clan of the orcs, famed for its blademasters. When the orcs fell under the power of demons, the Burning Blade fell further than most. In the {link:first-war}First War{/link} and the {link:second-war}Second War{/link} its warriors were a chaotic brotherhood, mad with battle and loyal to no one. They were let loose on the enemy only in times of great need.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}Two Paths.{/b} After the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, some blademasters of the clan joined {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}'s new {link:horde}Horde{/link} and swore to free themselves from demonic control. Others remained loyal to the demons. Under the {link:shadow-council}Shadow Council{/link}, the last of the orcish warlocks, these became a secret cult.
• {b}The Cult Spreads.{/b} The cult has welcomed members of other races, even humans and {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}, who share its devotion to the Legion.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The Burning Blade festers within {link:durotar}Durotar{/link} and {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link}. Its cultists hide in the caves of Durotar, at {link:skull-rock}Skull Rock{/link} and at Dustwind Cave, and they plot beneath {link:orgrimmar}Orgrimmar{/link} itself. In {link:desolace}Desolace{/link}, they hold the fortress of Thunder Axe, where their demon masters walk freely. The warriors of the {link:horde}Horde{/link} hunt them without rest, but the cult always seems to find new recruits.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "dark-iron-dwarves",
	title = "Dark Iron Dwarves",
	aliases = { "Dark Iron clan", "Dark Irons" },
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Dark Iron dwarves are the most feared of the three dwarven clans. They are masters of fire and dark magic. Two centuries ago they waged war on their kin, and in their defeat they unleashed a lord of flame who enslaved them. They dwell now in the depths of {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link}, bound to the service of the Firelord Ragnaros.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[Long ago, the {link:dwarves}dwarves{/link} of Khaz Modan were one people, ruled from {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} by the High King Modimus Anvilmar. When Modimus died, three clans fought for the throne: the Bronzebeards, the Wildhammers and the Dark Irons of the sorcerer-thane {link:ruins-of-thaurissan}Thaurissan{/link}. The Bronzebeards won and drove the others out. The Dark Irons went south and built the city of Thaurissan among the mountains.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The War of the Three Hammers.{/b} Some two hundred and thirty years before the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link}, the Dark Irons attacked both {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} and the Wildhammer seat of {link:grim-batol}Grim Batol{/link}. They were defeated at the gates of Ironforge.
• {b}The Coming of Ragnaros.{/b} In desperation, {link:ruins-of-thaurissan}Thaurissan{/link} sought a great power to aid him. He summoned Ragnaros, lord of the fire elementals. The Firelord's coming tore the land apart and created the {link:searing-gorge}Searing Gorge{/link} and the {link:burning-steppes}Burning Steppes{/link}. {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link} rose where the city had stood, and the Dark Irons became Ragnaros's slaves.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[Emperor Dagran {link:ruins-of-thaurissan}Thaurissan{/link} rules the Dark Irons from Shadowforge City, deep within {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link}. Ragnaros rules them all from the molten core below. Dark Iron forces raid the {link:searing-gorge}Searing Gorge{/link}, dig in the {link:badlands}Badlands{/link} and threaten the {link:wetlands}Wetlands{/link}. King {link:magni-bronzebeard}Magni Bronzebeard{/link} holds that his daughter Moira was carried off by the emperor, and he wants her back.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "steamwheedle-cartel",
	title = "Steamwheedle Cartel",
	aliases = { "Steamwheedle" },
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Steamwheedle Cartel is the greatest of the goblin trading companies. It owns ports and towns on both sides of the sea, and it keeps them open to any customer with gold. The Cartel has one loyalty: profit. Its neutrality has made it rich, and it guards that neutrality with hired muscle.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The goblins served the old {link:horde}Horde{/link} during the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}. The cartel's trade prince sold the orcs machines, maps, alchemy and zeppelins, and he built ships for Doomhammer's fleet. When the Horde was defeated, the goblins learned a lesson. It paid better to sell to both sides than to take either one.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}{link:booty-bay}Booty Bay{/link}.{/b} Before the {link:first-war}First War{/link}, the Cartel's goblins drove the trolls from a small port at the southern tip of {link:stranglethorn-vale}Stranglethorn{/link}. They made it their harbor of Booty Bay.
• {b}Across the Sea.{/b} In the years that followed, the Cartel built or claimed towns across {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}: {link:ratchet}Ratchet{/link} on the coast of {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link}, {link:gadgetzan}Gadgetzan{/link} in the desert of {link:tanaris}Tanaris{/link}, and {link:everlook}Everlook{/link} in the frozen north of {link:winterspring}Winterspring{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The Cartel's towns are havens where {link:orcs}orc{/link} and human may trade without drawing steel. Their bruisers keep the peace with a heavy hand. {link:baron-revilgaz}Baron Revilgaz{/link} rules {link:booty-bay}Booty Bay{/link}, {link:gazlowe}Gazlowe{/link} watches over {link:ratchet}Ratchet{/link}, and Mayor {link:marin-noggenfogger}Noggenfogger{/link} governs {link:gadgetzan}Gadgetzan{/link}. Each town struggles with pirates, rival companies and the wild lands around it. Many of its troubles come from the {link:venture-company}Venture Company{/link}, a goblin cartel with none of its manners.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "venture-company",
	title = "Venture Company",
	aliases = { "Venture Co." },
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Venture Company is a goblin cartel that strips the world of its riches. If a thing can be mined, cut down or pumped out of the ground, the Venture Company will take it, and it cares nothing for who lived there first. Its shredders and drills leave poisoned lakes and bare hills behind them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records the founding of the Venture Company. It is one of the goblin cartels of Undermine, and for many years it has been led by its president, Mogul Razdunk. Unlike the {link:steamwheedle-cartel}Steamwheedle Cartel{/link}, it keeps no neutral towns and makes no pretense of honor.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}In Kalimdor.{/b} The company came to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} after the {link:third-war}Third War{/link} and began to plunder it. It pumped oil in the {link:the-sludge-fen}Sludge Fen{/link} of {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link}. It cut the forests of {link:stonetalon-mountains}Stonetalon{/link}, and it dug into the cliffs of {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link} after the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} refused it the right.
• {b}In the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link}.{/b} In {link:stranglethorn-vale}Stranglethorn{/link}, the company cleared the jungle for timber and dug for rare crystals. It has also sold dark secrets to the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias Brotherhood{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The Venture Company is at work across the world. It fouls the wells of {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link} and tears at the forests of {link:stonetalon-mountains}Stonetalon{/link} with great machines. The {link:tauren}tauren{/link}, the night elves and the goblins of {link:steamwheedle-cartel}Steamwheedle{/link} all count it an enemy. Its overseers do not care, so long as the ore keeps coming.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "syndicate",
	title = "Syndicate",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Syndicate is a criminal league of the fallen nobles of {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac{/link}. It is made of thieves, assassins and brigands who serve lords without a kingdom. Its members prey upon the Alterac Mountains, the {link:hillsbrad-foothills}Hillsbrad Foothills{/link} and the {link:arathi-highlands}Arathi Highlands{/link}, and they dream of a crown that was taken from them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[In the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, {link:aiden-perenolde}Lord Aiden Perenolde{/link}, king of {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac{/link}, betrayed the {link:alliance}Alliance of Lordaeron{/link} to the {link:horde}Horde{/link}. When the war was over, Alterac was stripped of its crown and its lands. The nobles of Alterac never forgave the other kingdoms. Led by Perenolde's heir, {link:lord-aliden-perenolde}Lord Aliden Perenolde{/link}, they gathered thieves and sellswords and made them into the Syndicate.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}Before the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} Syndicate bandits were already at work in the woods of {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac{/link} before the plague struck {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}.
• {b}After the Fall.{/b} When Lordaeron fell, the Syndicate spread into the ruins it left behind. It seized {link:durnholde-keep}Durnholde Keep{/link} in {link:hillsbrad-foothills}Hillsbrad{/link} and much of {link:stromgarde-keep}Stromgarde{/link} in the {link:arathi-highlands}Arathi Highlands{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:lord-aliden-perenolde}Aliden Perenolde{/link} directs the Syndicate from {link:dandred-s-fold}Dandred's Fold{/link} in the {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac Mountains{/link}, and it holds the town of {link:strahnbrad}Strahnbrad{/link} as a fortress. {link:lord-falconcrest}Lord Falconcrest{/link} commands its forces in the ruins of {link:stromgarde-keep}Stromgarde{/link}. It steals horses and shipments from {link:southshore}Southshore{/link} and ambushes the soldiers of Stromgarde. The rogues of {link:ravenholdt-manor}Ravenholdt{/link} wage a long war against it, and the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} have put a price on the head of every one of its members.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "royal-apothecary-society",
	title = "Royal Apothecary Society",
	category = "group",
