	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Royal Apothecary Society is the order of alchemists who serve {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas Windrunner{/link}, the Banshee Queen of the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}. In the vaults beneath the {link:undercity}Undercity{/link}, its apothecaries brew poisons and plagues. Their stated purpose is a cure for undeath. Their true purpose is darker.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The Society was founded by {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas{/link} after the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} won their freedom from the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}. Its apothecaries set out to do what no living alchemist dared: to take the plague that had made the Forsaken and turn it into a weapon of their own. The apothecaries set up their laboratories in the {link:the-apothecarium}Apothecarium{/link}, beneath the {link:royal-quarter}Royal Quarter{/link} of the {link:undercity}Undercity{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Cure and the Plague.{/b} When the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} joined the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, its other peoples believed that the apothecaries were seeking a cure for their condition. In truth, the Society's first work was a new plague, meant to destroy the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}.
• {b}Other Arts.{/b} The Society has also raised dead horses to serve as steeds for the Forsaken, and it sends its members far and wide to gather new ingredients.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[In the {link:the-apothecarium}Apothecarium{/link}, {link:master-apothecary-faranell}Master Apothecary Faranell{/link} oversees the work of the new plague, and the Society's agents test it in the fields of {link:hillsbrad-foothills}Hillsbrad{/link} and elsewhere. Its apothecaries serve in every {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} outpost. Their allies in the {link:horde}Horde{/link} watch them with growing unease.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "darkspear-trolls",
	title = "Darkspear Trolls",
	aliases = { "Darkspear tribe", "Darkspear" },
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Darkspear are a tribe of jungle {link:trolls}trolls{/link} who stand with the {link:horde}Horde{/link}. They were outcasts and wanderers until {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} saved them from destruction. Now they are the orcs' most loyal allies. They are hunters, witch doctors and fierce warriors, and they owe their survival to the Warchief.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The Darkspear were once a tribe of the Gurubashi, the jungle trolls of {link:stranglethorn-vale}Stranglethorn{/link}. When the Gurubashi Empire fell apart, its tribes turned on one another, and the Darkspear were driven out. They made a new home on islands in the southern seas.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Rescue.{/b} When {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}'s fleet was driven onto their island by a storm, the Darkspear were in grave danger. {link:humans}Humans{/link} of {link:kul-tiras}Kul Tiras{/link} and murlocs of the sea were attacking them. Thrall fought beside them, and their leader, Sen'jin, was taken. Sen'jin died a captive of the murlocs, but he had foreseen that Thrall would lead his people to a new home.
• {b}Kalimdor.{/b} The Darkspear sailed with the {link:horde}Horde{/link} to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} and settled on the {link:echo-isles}Echo Isles{/link} off the coast of {link:durotar}Durotar{/link}.
• {b}{link:zalazane}Zalazane{/link}.{/b} A witch doctor named Zalazane turned on his tribe. With dark voodoo, he enslaved many of the trolls of the Echo Isles and drove the rest from their homes.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The free Darkspear have settled on the coast of {link:durotar}Durotar{/link}, in the village they named for Sen'jin. Sen'jin's son, {link:vol-jin}Vol'jin{/link}, leads them and stands at {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}'s side in {link:orgrimmar}Orgrimmar{/link}. {link:zalazane}Zalazane{/link} still rules the {link:echo-isles}Echo Isles{/link}, and the Darkspear mean to take them back.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "kingdom-of-ironforge",
	title = "Kingdom of Ironforge",
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Kingdom of Ironforge is the realm of the Bronzebeard {link:dwarves}dwarves{/link}. Its capital is carved into the heart of a mountain in {link:dun-morogh}Dun Morogh{/link}, and its forges have burned for thousands of years. It is a kingdom of miners, smiths, engineers and scholars. It is also one of the two pillars of the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The dwarves say that they were shaped from stone in ages past. Their oldest city is {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}, and for a long time all dwarves were ruled from it. When High King Modimus Anvilmar died, the Bronzebeard, Wildhammer and Dark Iron clans fought over the throne. The Bronzebeards held Ironforge and drove the other two clans out. In the War of the Three Hammers, they defeated the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} at the city's gates.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}Friends of Men.{/b} Explorers from {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} reached Khaz Modan long ago. The dwarves and humans became friends and traded knowledge of smithing, engineering and magic.
• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} When the {link:horde}Horde{/link} overran Khaz Modan, {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} itself held out. The dwarves joined the {link:alliance}Alliance of Lordaeron{/link}, and they did not forget who stood with them.
• {b}The {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} King {link:magni-bronzebeard}Magni Bronzebeard{/link}'s brother {link:muradin-bronzebeard}Muradin Bronzebeard{/link} went to Northrend with Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} and never returned. The dwarves mourn him as lost.
• {b}The Fall of Gnomeregan.{/b} When {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link} was lost, Magni gave its surviving {link:gnomes}gnomes{/link} a home in his city.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:magni-bronzebeard}King Magni{/link} rules {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}. His younger brother {link:brann-bronzebeard}Brann Bronzebeard{/link} roams the world for the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link}. The gnomes of {link:gelbin-mekkatorque}Gelbin Mekkatorque{/link} live in {link:tinker-town}Tinker Town{/link}, in the city's heart. Dwarven soldiers guard {link:loch-modan}Loch Modan{/link} and the passes of the south. The {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} threaten from {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock{/link}, and Magni grieves for his daughter Moira, who he says was taken by their emperor.]=],
		},
	},
})
